# Snyk temporary OAuth

`.github/workflows/security-scans.yml` runs Snyk with **SNYK_OAUTH_TOKEN** (from `snyk auth`, ~1h expiry). Long-lived fallback: **SNYK_TOKEN** API token in repo secrets.

## On any Snyk request

1. Remind OAuth expires ~1h; refresh: `snyk auth` then `scripts/refresh-snyk-oauth-secret.ps1`.
2. Offer to run the refresh script when CI/auth fails or before scan work.
3. MCP `user-Snyk` may error without valid local auth; CLI + CI workflow is primary.
4. Keep Snyk in security-scans.yml alongside other scanners (Trivy, Semgrep, Gitleaks, npm audit, etc.).
